in one pound." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from pounds to ounces. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we multiply the number of pounds  by $16:$  \n\n$$\n2\\times 16=32\n$$\n\nSo, $2$ pounds is the same as $32$ ounces. Now, to find the unit price per ounce, we divide the total price by $32:$\n\n$$\n4.80÷32=0.15\n$$\n\nTherefore, the raisins cost $\\$0.15$ per ounce."} :step/id #uuid "222ef67b-ec25-5cef-b693-111a09425fec" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575630}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575645 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575612 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2be12b11-3652-52e4-adce-89e1e7625e58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$8.00$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575021} {:answer/id #uuid "2ed0b6cc-dc15-5ab5-8bc7-84da3585b4ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$9.60$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575027} {:answer/id #uuid "3497fac9-fc4e-56a7-bdbf-3df6bb29d82a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$12.80$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575038} {:answer/id #uuid "5b0c9344-df9c-5f3f-b871-4631ff371574" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$10.20$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575110} {:answer/id #uuid "d62a7cd4-5580-5f49-81c7-8e925474945a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$14.40$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575331}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575038} :answer-field/id #uuid "44ddfc6b-4838-5599-a86f-bf8221237272" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e3c42dde-368f-51a4-a96b-0c5d0e222f8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-354923" :question/problem "A scientist bought $1$ fluid ounce of a chemical solution and paid $\\$1.60$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that there are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup.  \n\nSince the price is $\\$1.60$ per fluid ounce, to find the price per cup, we multiply by $8:$\n\n$$\n1.60\\times 8=12.80\n$$\n\nTherefore, the chemical solution costs $\\$12.80$ per cup."} :step/id #uuid "3a2423d0-c8dc-5183-b7f8-6ca7246149ac" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575678}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575541 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09f9eee1-0098-5229-b9ce-e4b65237d12f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$0.24$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574966} {:answer/id #uuid "1e0f4944-55fa-5715-8483-aaea1dc8f44d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$2.50$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574995} {:answer/id #uuid "210351d0-1105-53ce-b4c8-02147d3c6fd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$1.92$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575004} {:answer/id #uuid "42e3a724-292a-58b1-ac69-9a6cb1767985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$2.10$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575065} {:answer/id #uuid "747d7d4b-1fd2-5d3e-86b4-da9429862057" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$1.75$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575162}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575004} :answer-field/id #uuid "ffbd78f3-a124-58f1-9f81-8177785c5280" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4b574a7a-bdad-59b8-aadb-22d876ef5c0b" :question/math-academy-id "q-354928" :question/problem "Emily filled a container with $48$ fluid ounces of juice and paid $\\$11.52$ for it. What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$     \n\n$$\n48÷8=6\n$$\n\nSo, $48$ fluid ounces is the same as $6$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $6:$ \n\n$$\n11.52÷6=1.92\n$$\n\nTherefore, the juice costs $\\$1.92$ per cup."} :step/id #uuid "b27410e4-9002-576a-ac62-f2734f5665e2"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575687 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575576 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51be7f7b-234a-535f-8314-06a596ba3268" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$15.60$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575090} {:answer/id #uuid "7abd7d8f-b5de-5cfc-b3bf-1a23c149a745" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$12.25$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575171} {:answer/id #uuid "826c5023-ef86-5ab9-acaa-ec789d00fac6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$16.80$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575182} {:answer/id #uuid "9d87d5ae-077e-5462-9e51-8ecda822620f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$18.20$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575220} {:answer/id #uuid "a0bb0036-fab5-5d80-ba7d-7ad30685b95d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\$14.75$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575230}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186575182} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1a6bc1-e6b7-5531-84ae-b676cb38f400" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186575501}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "947d34a3-027e-5d38-b8d1-e6f3a1b0d3d2" :question/math-academy-id "q-354916" :question/problem "Emily bought $1$ foot of gold wire and paid $\\$5.60$ for it. What's the unit price per yard?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  